---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<Base title="About" section="about" description="What this site is, what it isn't, and how to get in touch.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="About" title="A workshop, not a portfolio">
    This site is a place to put things I've made and things I've learned, so that other people can use them.
  </PageHead>

  <section class="wrap body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What you'll find</h2>
      <p>
        Browser tools that do one job well. Retro games rebuilt for a modern browser. Notes on
        things I'm interested in, and guides for things I've had to figure out more than once.
        There is no single theme, and that is deliberate.
      </p>

      <h2>What you won't</h2>
      <p>
        Photos, family, or personal details. This is about interests, facts, instructions and
        experiences, nothing more.
      </p>

      <h2 id="livia-karsten">Livia Karsten</h2>
      <p>
        Away from the browser, I design and sell fashion watches under the name
        <a href="https://liviakarsten.com" rel="me">Livia Karsten</a>
        (<a href="https://liviakarsten.co.za">liviakarsten.co.za</a> in South Africa). It started
        in 2014 as an idea and some rough models, and took a long road through 3D modelling,
        CNC machining, moulding, an online configurator, photography and market stalls before it
        became a finished product. The story of how it was made, and a guide for each thing I had
        to learn along the way, are coming to this site.
      </p>

      <h2>How it's built</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. The tools and games run entirely in your
        browser. The only thing counted is page views;
        there are no accounts and nothing you do here is uploaded anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>[Add a contact method here — an email alias, a form service, or a link.]</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .body { padding-bottom: 72px; }
</style>
